                <pb facs="1041" n="913" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg913"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 689.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr.
                            Baker</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-04-22"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 22,
                        1885</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 59.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Adverting to my instructions to your No.
                    51, of March 24 last, and No. 56, of the 9th instant, I have now to transmit for
                    your further information a copy of a dispatch from the United States consul at
                    La Guayra, No. 202, of the 16th ultimo, giving additional incidents relative to
                    the casualty sustained by the American vessel Lanie Cobb, of Bangor, Maine, in
                    the port of La Guayra.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d689-a1.xml" xpointer="d689-a1"/>
            </div>
